Subject: [PATCH] fix(goals): a goal the owner closed stays closed; no members
 note on a closing turn (RW-012 B)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MTR #7, goal 20759: the owner wrote „ეს მოგვარდა, დახურე." The goal was still
open while that run closed it, so the „members on Netai were not offered" note
(2908) fired. The model promised to write to two more people, the goal was
open again, and a day later it woke and wrote to the owner.

Two server rules close it:
- The members note is out of place on any line that closes or settles
  („მოგვარდა", „დახურე", „ვხურავ დანარჩენ კითხვებს", "solved, close it"…), and
  on any run that called finish_task, whatever the goal's status in that
  moment.
- update_task may set a CLOSED goal back to open only when the owner's own
  line in that run asks to go on („გააგრძელე", „ხელახლა გახსენი", "reopen",
  "resume"…). Otherwise it is refused before anything is written, with a
  reason code; no new model prose.

DONE WHEN: RW-012 B; a goal closed by the owner („მოგვარდა, დახურე") stays
closed, gets no second message after the closing line, and never wakes.

